      "id": 1,
      "text": "San Simon was founded in early 1859 as the first Butterfield Overland stagecoach station on the Arizona–New Mexico border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sansimonaz.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The arrival of the Southern Pacific Railroad in the 1880s turned the stagecoach stop into a bustling railroad town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sansimonaz.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Bowie National Historic Site, just north of San Simon, preserves the site where Apache resistance once stood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://scientificmagz.blog/san-simon-az-cochise-county-guide"
    },
    {
